00:34:40.860 --> 00:34:41.860
Well, here's the deal.
好吧，情况是这样的。

808
00:34:42.160 --> 00:34:46.760
Randy even went to extra measures to make sure the cat would be fine when they were going to drop it on my desk.
兰迪甚至采取了额外措施，确保在他们要把猫扔到我桌子上时，猫会安然无恙。

809
00:34:47.240 --> 00:34:59.440
He and the animal trainers and our stunt guy, Eric Sulke, they came up with this huge inflatable safety airbag that would decelerate and gently catch the falling cat.
他和动物训练师以及我们的特技演员埃里克·苏尔克，他们想出了一个巨大的充气安全气囊，可以减速并轻柔地接住落下的猫。

810
00:34:59.440 --> 00:35:01.920
It was described as like falling into feathers.
它被形容为就像掉进羽毛堆里一样。

811
00:35:02.240 --> 00:35:06.380
And we did some practice runs and the trainers signed off on it.
我们做了一些练习，训练师们也认可了。

812
00:35:06.480 --> 00:35:07.040
It was fine.
没问题的。

813
00:35:07.280 --> 00:35:09.180
The cat wasn't traumatized at all.
猫一点也没有受到惊吓。

814
00:35:09.360 --> 00:35:14.540
They hid this airbag in the corner of my accounting desk with like papers and stuff.
他们把这个气囊藏在我会计桌的角落里，用文件之类的东西盖住。

815
00:35:14.660 --> 00:35:17.880
But there was a cat airbag on my desk.
但我的桌子上确实有个猫用气囊。

816
00:35:17.880 --> 00:35:18.440
Okay.
好的。

817
00:35:18.740 --> 00:35:22.660
And the ceiling panel had breakaway foam rubber.
天花板的嵌板用的是易碎的泡沫橡胶。

818
00:35:22.820 --> 00:35:23.380
All right.
行吧。

819
00:35:23.540 --> 00:35:25.580
So it was all very cushy, cushy.
所以一切都非常非常柔软舒适。

820
00:35:25.580 --> 00:35:27.240
But now –
但现在——

821
00:35:27.240 --> 00:35:32.360
I just want to say they did all of this and then gave Rain a real blowtorch.
我只想说，他们做了所有这些保护措施，然后却给了雷恩一个真正的喷火器。

822
00:35:32.420 --> 00:35:32.880
I know.
我知道。

823
00:35:33.260 --> 00:35:37.860
They had an inflatable airbag cushion for this enormous cat.
他们为这只巨大的猫准备了充气气囊垫。

824
00:35:38.020 --> 00:35:42.940
But now, Jenna, enter in the people that make fake animals.
但现在，珍娜，那些制作仿真动物的人登场了。

825
00:35:43.240 --> 00:35:44.080
I'm scared.
我好怕。

826
00:35:44.380 --> 00:35:45.800
I found them fascinating.
我觉得他们很迷人。

827
00:35:45.800 --> 00:35:51.660
So, like, you know, if you have a show like CSI and there's a dead body, these are your people.
就像，你知道，如果你拍像《犯罪现场调查》这样的剧，里面有尸体，这些人就是负责制作的。

828
00:35:51.840 --> 00:35:52.620
They make fake humans.
他们制作仿真人类。

829
00:35:52.800 --> 00:35:53.700
They make fake animals.
他们制作仿真动物。

830
00:35:54.280 --> 00:36:00.280
Jenna, they had to meticulously match the exact cat that we were tossing in the ceiling.
珍娜，他们必须一丝不苟地还原我们要扔进天花板的那只猫。

831
00:36:00.660 --> 00:36:02.240
And it was a rush job.
而且时间非常紧迫。

832
00:36:02.780 --> 00:36:05.540
Randy said this fake cat cost $12,000.
兰迪说这只假猫花了12000美元。

833
00:36:05.940 --> 00:36:06.940
Oh, my God!
天哪！

834
00:36:06.940 --> 00:36:07.800
I know.
我知道。

835
00:36:07.980 --> 00:36:13.640
And I want you to know that thing was one of the scariest things I've ever seen, held or touched.
我想让你知道，那东西是我见过、拿过或摸过的最可怕的东西之一。

836
00:36:13.900 --> 00:36:17.240
First of all, it had these yellow eyes that would just look at you.
首先，它有那种会一直盯着你看的黄眼睛。

837
00:36:17.480 --> 00:36:19.820
And then the fur felt real.
而且毛摸起来很真实。

838
00:36:20.020 --> 00:36:22.740
But when you picked it up, it was gelatinous.
但当你把它拿起来时，它却是胶状的。

839
00:36:22.920 --> 00:36:25.320
So, like, flop, like, as you held it.
所以，就像，当你拿着它时，它会晃荡。

840
00:36:25.380 --> 00:36:25.740
Oh, my God.
天哪。

841
00:36:25.760 --> 00:36:29.700
Like, imagine, like, flopping a towel over your arm, a big, thick towel.
就像，想象一下，把一条毛巾搭在手臂上，一条又大又厚的毛巾。

842
00:36:29.860 --> 00:36:30.940
It was, like, smushy.
它就是那种软塌塌的感觉。

843
00:36:31.120 --> 00:36:31.860
It was frightening.
太吓人了。

844
00:36:32.440 --> 00:36:34.940
I – we started kind of pranking with it.
我——我们开始用它搞恶作剧了。

845
00:36:34.940 --> 00:36:38.180
Like, I said it on Oscar's desk, and he walked up, and he was like, oh, God!
比如，我把它放在奥斯卡的桌子上，他走过来，然后他就说，噢，天哪！

846
00:36:38.780 --> 00:36:43.720
I had to, like, start covering its face with a piece of paper because the thing was so creepy to look at.
我不得不开始用一张纸盖住它的脸，因为它看起来太诡异了。

847
00:36:43.900 --> 00:36:44.860
Where is it now?
它现在在哪？

848
00:36:44.860 --> 00:36:45.700
I don't know.
我不知道。

849
00:36:45.860 --> 00:36:46.400
Who has it?
谁拿着它？

850
00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:48.980
NBC owns it somewhere, right?
NBC把它收在什么地方了吧，对吧？

851
00:36:49.140 --> 00:36:50.080
They paid for it.
他们为此付了钱。

852
00:36:50.420 --> 00:36:52.280
By the way, this is just the cat stuff.
顺便说一下，这还只是猫的部分。

853
00:36:52.280 --> 00:36:56.740
We haven't even gotten to the fact that Oscar has a whole bit he has to do.
我们还没提到奥斯卡还得演一段戏呢。

854
00:36:56.840 --> 00:36:57.300
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

855
00:36:57.480 --> 00:36:57.720
Right?
对吧？

856
00:36:58.000 --> 00:37:02.100
So, when we actually got to the day to shoot the stunt, I go over to the drawer.
所以，当我们真正到了拍摄特技的那天，我走到抽屉前。

857
00:37:02.380 --> 00:37:03.560
I pull out the cat.
我把猫拿出来。

858
00:37:03.560 --> 00:37:07.920
Now, they said my dialogue and everything, I still had to be yelling, okay?
他们说我的台词和所有东西，我还是得大喊大叫，明白吗？

859
00:37:08.360 --> 00:37:12.600
So, I open the drawer, and you'll hear in the take I say to the cat, it's okay.
所以我打开抽屉，你会听到在拍摄中我对猫说，没事的。

860
00:37:12.860 --> 00:37:15.140
Like, I'm trying to, like, be like, I'm not a bad person.
就像，我试图表现得，我不是个坏人。

861
00:37:15.500 --> 00:37:25.840
I lift up this enormous cat, and then I have to go to my spot where Oscar's going in the roof, and they wanted – so they could do that swishy cut –
我抱起这只巨大的猫，然后我得走到奥斯卡要进屋顶的位置，他们想要——这样他们就能做那种快速剪辑——

862
00:37:25.840 --> 00:37:26.060
Yeah.
是啊。

863
00:37:26.200 --> 00:37:27.560
They wanted me to take the cat.
他们要我抱着猫。

864
00:37:27.740 --> 00:37:28.740
I'm holding it to my cheSt.
我把它抱在胸前。

865
00:37:28.940 --> 00:37:36.120
They wanted me to swing the cat back behind me and then swing it up over my head and stop.
他们要我把猫向后甩，然后甩过头顶并停住。

866
00:37:36.340 --> 00:37:37.540
This is the real cat.
这是真的猫。

867
00:37:37.660 --> 00:37:38.560
The real cat.
真的猫。

868
00:37:38.700 --> 00:37:38.940
Okay.
好吧。

869
00:37:39.280 --> 00:37:41.760
The real cat gets the swinging motion.
真的猫要经历甩动的动作。

870
00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:42.800
Swinging okay.
甩动没问题。

871
00:37:43.100 --> 00:37:43.840
Swinging okay.
甩动没问题。

872
00:37:43.840 --> 00:37:44.640
Swinging approved.
甩动已获批。

873
00:37:44.860 --> 00:37:45.660
Swinging approved.
甩动已获批。

874
00:37:45.660 --> 00:37:49.300
While I'm yelling, I only weigh 82 pounds!
当我大喊大叫时，我才82磅重！

875
00:37:49.780 --> 00:37:50.280
Right?
对吧？

876
00:37:50.640 --> 00:37:52.260
I'm sure the cat loved that.
我敢肯定猫很喜欢那样。

877
00:37:52.520 --> 00:37:53.680
You know what cats love?
你知道猫喜欢什么吗？

878
00:37:53.940 --> 00:37:54.500
Screaming.
尖叫。

879
00:37:54.780 --> 00:37:55.480
And swinging.
还有甩动。

880
00:37:55.820 --> 00:37:56.000
Yeah.
是啊。

881
00:37:56.420 --> 00:37:58.360
This cat probably weighed 20 pounds.
这只猫大概有20磅重。

882
00:37:58.500 --> 00:38:00.160
I'm not exaggerating at all.
我一点都没夸张。

883
00:38:00.200 --> 00:38:00.840
It was enormous.
它太巨大了。

884
00:38:01.500 --> 00:38:04.620
Just the swinging and getting it to my stopping point.
光是甩动它并把它带到我的停止点。

885
00:38:04.780 --> 00:38:05.400
It was like –
就像是——

886
00:38:05.400 --> 00:38:07.500
I was like, oh, God.
我当时想，噢，天哪。

887
00:38:08.260 --> 00:38:10.880
And then I stop, and I hold it in the air.
然后我停住，把它举在空中。

888
00:38:11.280 --> 00:38:11.680
Freeze.
定住。

889
00:38:12.060 --> 00:38:15.460
Then they yell, cut, and in comes my stunt woman in the same outfit.
然后他们喊停，我的替身演员穿着同样的衣服进来了。

890
00:38:15.460 --> 00:38:16.380
She takes real cat.
她接过真的猫。

891
00:38:16.540 --> 00:38:17.520
She holds it in the air.
她把它举在空中。

892
00:38:17.700 --> 00:38:26.540
I step away because what she's going to do with the cat, Jenna, is kind of do the second motion where it appears like she's tossing, but she doesn't toss the cat.
我走开了，因为她接下来要对猫做的事，珍娜，就是做第二个动作，看起来像是她在扔猫，但她并没有真的扔。

893
00:38:26.740 --> 00:38:27.140
Okay.
好的。

894
00:38:27.300 --> 00:38:30.500
But she kind of gives it a little air, but not a lot of air.
但她给了它一点腾空感，不过没多少。

895
00:38:30.500 --> 00:38:34.320
And this was like, they don't want you to get all scratched up.
这就像是，他们不想让你被抓伤。

896
00:38:34.420 --> 00:38:36.640
She knows how to give like a little thing.
她知道怎么做那种小动作。

897
00:38:36.640 --> 00:38:36.920
Yeah.
是啊。

898
00:38:37.140 --> 00:38:39.200
They had to give the idea of the motion.
他们必须传达出那种动作的感觉。

899
00:38:39.360 --> 00:38:39.540
Yeah.
是啊。

900
00:38:39.720 --> 00:38:40.000
Right?
对吧？

901
00:38:40.220 --> 00:38:40.480
Right.
没错。

902
00:38:40.600 --> 00:38:41.680
More than my swing.
比我的秋千还多。

903
00:38:41.960 --> 00:38:42.300
Got it.
明白了。

904
00:38:42.420 --> 00:38:42.640
Okay?
好吗？

905
00:38:42.840 --> 00:38:48.000
And then, of course, we had to get a take where I had to take Fakie Cat and do the same motion as the stunt woman.
然后，当然了，我们还得拍一个镜头，我必须拿着假猫，做出和替身演员一样的动作。

906
00:38:48.140 --> 00:38:51.080
I had to watch her and toss Fakie Cat in the ceiling.
我得盯着她，把假猫扔到天花板里。

907
00:38:51.540 --> 00:38:51.980
Right?
对吧？

908
00:38:52.240 --> 00:38:52.540
Yes.
是的。

909
00:38:52.620 --> 00:38:54.260
They pieced all of that together.
他们把所有这些片段拼在了一起。

910
00:38:54.900 --> 00:39:04.400
So, Jenna, I had talked to Jeff Blitz about this moment a while back because I distinctly remember when we filmed it, two cats coming out of the ceiling instead of one.
所以，珍娜，我很久以前就和杰夫·布里茨聊过这个瞬间，因为我清楚地记得拍摄当时，有两只猫从天花板里掉出来，而不是一只。

911
00:39:04.640 --> 00:39:04.960
How?
怎么会？

912
00:39:05.060 --> 00:39:06.780
How did two cats come out?
怎么会有两只猫掉出来？

913
00:39:07.100 --> 00:39:08.040
That's my memory.
我是这么记得的。

914
00:39:08.040 --> 00:39:09.500
And I was like, wait, am I crazy?
当时我就想，等等，是我疯了吗？

915
00:39:09.660 --> 00:39:11.520
And I talked to Dean Holland, who edited it.
于是我问了负责剪辑的迪恩·霍兰德。

916
00:39:11.540 --> 00:39:14.460
And I was like, Dean, did you have to CGI out one cat?
我问他，迪恩，你是不是用电脑特效删掉了一只猫？

917
00:39:14.540 --> 00:39:16.060
Because I know two cats came down.
因为我记得明明有两只猫掉下来。

918
00:39:16.080 --> 00:39:17.560
I remember seeing two cats.
我记得我看到了两只猫。

919
00:39:17.900 --> 00:39:18.860
He was like, no.
他说没有。

920
00:39:18.860 --> 00:39:22.520
And so I talked to Jeff Blitz, and he goes, yes, Angela, two cats came down.
后来我找杰夫·布里茨确认，他说，没错，安吉拉，确实有两只猫掉下来了。

921
00:39:22.720 --> 00:39:23.620
And I was like, what?
我当时就惊了，什么？

922
00:39:23.780 --> 00:39:29.940
He said, on the take we used, the trainer that was supposed to catch the Fakie Cat missed.
他说，在我们用的那个镜头里，本该接住假猫的驯兽师没接住。

923
00:39:30.360 --> 00:39:30.780
Oh.
噢。

924
00:39:31.140 --> 00:39:36.660
And so then, on action, Fakie Cat came out the other side and real cat.
所以，在喊开始后，假猫从另一边掉出来，然后真猫也掉出来了。

925
00:39:37.540 --> 00:39:39.260
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

926
00:39:39.420 --> 00:39:40.900
Two cats hit the desk.
两只猫都砸在了桌子上。

927
00:39:41.280 --> 00:39:46.420
And Jeff said, luckily, the way the camera was positioned, it only caught one cat.
杰夫说，幸运的是，摄像机的位置刚好只拍到了一只猫。

928
00:39:46.420 --> 00:39:50.300
And I think it's the real cat when you watch.
而且我觉得你现在看的时候，那应该是那只真猫。

929
00:39:50.480 --> 00:39:52.040
It looks like a real cat comes down.
看起来确实像是一只真猫掉下来了。

930
00:39:52.060 --> 00:39:55.360
Yeah, because it hits and it kind of runs off, whereas Fakie Cat just would have gone plop.
没错，因为它落地后还跑开了，而假猫的话应该只会“啪”地一声掉在那儿。

931
00:39:55.700 --> 00:39:56.160
Yes.
是的。

932
00:39:56.720 --> 00:39:57.020
Right?
对吧？

933
00:39:57.420 --> 00:39:57.880
Yes.
是的。

934
00:39:58.320 --> 00:39:59.740
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

935
00:40:00.100 --> 00:40:04.500
One cat went up, two cats came down, but we got the shot.
一只猫上去，两只猫下来，但我们最终拍到了想要的镜头。

936
00:40:04.760 --> 00:40:09.580
It took all those people and all that maneuvering, but it made it in the episode.
虽然动用了那么多人，费了那么多周折，但它最终还是出现在了剧集里。

937
00:40:09.940 --> 00:40:11.440
Angela, that is amazing.
安吉拉，这太神奇了。

938
00:40:11.880 --> 00:40:14.440
I did not know all the details of that story.
我之前完全不知道这个故事的细节。

939
00:40:15.440 --> 00:40:16.800
I was on the edge of my seat.
我听得心都提到嗓子眼了。

940
00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:17.940
I absolutely loved that.
我太喜欢这个故事了。

941
00:40:18.760 --> 00:40:23.560
You guys, the crazy thing is it took me that long to tell that story, but it happened in five seconds.
伙计们，最疯狂的是，我花了这么久才讲完这个故事，但它其实只发生了五秒钟。

942
00:40:23.580 --> 00:40:24.160
Oh, my God.
天哪。

943
00:40:24.200 --> 00:40:26.680
When we actually filmed it, it was so quick.
我们实际拍摄的时候，动作非常快。

944
00:40:27.100 --> 00:40:32.100
So it was like, me, drawer, cat, swing, step out, Fakie Cat.
当时就是：我、抽屉、猫、秋千、走出来、假猫。

945
00:40:32.320 --> 00:40:34.180
Oh, my God, two cats, react to one.
天哪，两只猫，还要对其中一只做出反应。

946
00:40:37.500 --> 00:40:43.800
Well, you mentioned that there was something else going on during all this, which was Oscar going in and out of the ceiling.
嗯，你提到过当时还有别的事情在发生，就是奥斯卡进出天花板的那段。

947
00:40:43.800 --> 00:40:46.540
Yes, that was a whole other ordeal.
是的，那是另一场折磨。

948
00:40:47.120 --> 00:41:00.840
Randy told us that that part of the stunt of getting Oscar up into the ceiling was the other most challenging part of the stunt because there was nothing to climb into in the way that our set was built.
兰迪告诉我们，让奥斯卡进入天花板的那部分特技，是整个特技中最具挑战性的另一部分，因为我们的布景结构根本没法让人爬进去。

949
00:41:00.840 --> 00:41:07.440
Like, the actual lightweight drop ceiling, it was suspended from cables.
就像那种实际的轻质吊顶，它是用缆绳悬挂着的。

950
00:41:07.840 --> 00:41:10.300
Yeah, very thin rigging wires.
没错，非常细的索具钢丝。

951
00:41:10.440 --> 00:41:16.540
It was Fakie ceiling, guys, because our set was inside a humongous soundstage.
那是假天花板，伙计们，因为我们的布景是在一个巨大的摄影棚里。

952
00:41:16.780 --> 00:41:17.000
Yeah.
没错。

953
00:41:17.000 --> 00:41:20.660
So, actually, above the Dunder Mifflin offices was just air.
所以实际上，邓德·米夫林办公室上方只有空气。

954
00:41:20.840 --> 00:41:25.980
If you walked outside, you could look up and just see these wires holding Fakie ceiling.
如果你走到外面，抬头就能看到那些支撑着假天花板的电线。

955
00:41:26.260 --> 00:41:26.500
Yeah.
没错。

956
00:41:26.760 --> 00:41:39.060
So he said in the weeks prior to filming this, our production designer, Michael Gallenberg, and construction coordinator, Tim James, had to completely re-engineer the ceiling.
他说在拍摄前几周，我们的美术指导迈克尔·加伦伯格和施工协调员蒂姆·詹姆斯不得不彻底重新设计了天花板。

957
00:41:39.320 --> 00:41:42.880
They had to, like, build rafters, basically, that we didn't have, right?
他们基本上得搭建出我们原本没有的椽子，对吧？

958
00:41:42.880 --> 00:41:49.200
Yeah, and it had to be enough to support not just Oscar, but all of the stunt personnel.
是的，而且它不仅要能支撑奥斯卡，还要支撑所有的特技人员。

959
00:41:49.500 --> 00:42:02.040
He said on the day, there were two stunt coordinators, the animal people, Oscar, Oscar's stunt double, and an NBC universal safety coordinator all up in the ceiling.
他说在那天，有两名特技协调员、动物工作人员、奥斯卡、奥斯卡的特技替身，还有一名NBC环球的安全协调员，全都待在天花板上。

960
00:42:02.200 --> 00:42:04.420
Can you imagine that guy's day at work?
你能想象那家伙的工作日吗？

961
00:42:04.580 --> 00:42:05.340
I can't.
我无法想象。

962
00:42:05.400 --> 00:42:07.100
Like, he's not normally with us.
他平时又不跟我们在一起。

963
00:42:07.240 --> 00:42:09.260
He's just up in our ceiling now.
现在他却待在我们的天花板里。

964
00:42:09.480 --> 00:42:12.740
I can tell you that I had to look up into the ceiling.
我可以告诉你，我当时不得不抬头看天花板。

965
00:42:12.880 --> 00:42:14.160
And it looked crowded.
看起来确实很拥挤。

966
00:42:14.480 --> 00:42:17.500
I get why someone might have missed a cat as it flew up there.
我明白为什么有人会错过一只飞上去的猫了。

967
00:42:19.400 --> 00:42:22.100
Well, we got a fan question from Alex M.
好吧，我们收到一个来自亚历克斯·M的粉丝提问。

968
00:42:22.460 --> 00:42:25.160
Did Oscar really fall through the ceiling?
奥斯卡真的从天花板上掉下来了吗？

969
00:42:26.140 --> 00:42:26.540
Yes.
是的。

970
00:42:26.840 --> 00:42:28.100
Well, yes and no, right?
嗯，算是也算不是吧，对吧？

971
00:42:28.340 --> 00:42:32.020
We pulled it off using both Oscar and a stunt double, right, Ange?
我们是结合了奥斯卡本人和特技替身完成的，对吧，安吉？

972
00:42:32.100 --> 00:42:32.280
Yeah.
没错。

973
00:42:32.440 --> 00:42:37.440
So I reached out to Oscar, and I was like, Oscar, you got to tell us everything about the ceiling.
所以我联系了奥斯卡，我说，奥斯卡，你得把关于天花板的一切都告诉我们。

974
00:42:37.580 --> 00:42:39.080
I guess he gets asked this a lot.
我想他经常被问到这个问题。

975
00:42:39.600 --> 00:42:41.320
And he sent in this audio clip.
于是他发来了这段音频。

976
00:42:41.320 --> 00:42:42.900
But I had a stuntman.
但我有一个替身演员。

977
00:42:43.100 --> 00:42:44.640
I had a Moroccan.
他是个摩洛哥人。

978
00:42:44.940 --> 00:42:48.000
He was – I think he was from Morocco.
他是——我想他是摩洛哥来的。

979
00:42:48.180 --> 00:42:52.120
He was from Cirque du Soleil.
他来自太阳马戏团。

980
00:42:52.400 --> 00:42:53.860
He was a little shorter than me.
他比我稍微矮一点。

981
00:42:54.160 --> 00:42:55.480
And he was a stuntman.
他是个特技演员。

982
00:42:55.480 --> 00:43:02.200
And I think he was jumping out from the hole and doing wonderful tumbles when he hit the ground.
我想他是从洞里跳出来，落地时还做了很棒的翻滚动作。

983
00:43:02.580 --> 00:43:03.980
I did half of it.
我完成了一半。

984
00:43:04.060 --> 00:43:05.420
He did the really hard part.
他完成了真正困难的部分。

985
00:43:05.740 --> 00:43:07.960
It was a very funny scene, very complicated.
那是一个非常有趣的场景，非常复杂。

986
00:43:08.640 --> 00:43:18.700
I remember in one of the shots, I made Steve laugh because one of the ways that I was coming down from the roof, on one of them, they had a big bar up there,
我记得在其中一个镜头里，我把史蒂夫逗笑了，因为我从屋顶下来的方式之一，其中一种，他们在上面装了一根大横杆，

987
00:43:18.800 --> 00:43:20.560
and it lowered me slowly through the hole.
然后把我慢慢地从洞里降下来。

988
00:43:21.100 --> 00:43:22.740
And that was a funny way to come down.
那是一种很有趣的下来方式。

989
00:43:22.740 --> 00:43:26.660
And when I made eye contact with Steve, just hanging there with a straight face, of course, he laughed.
当我跟史蒂夫对视时，我面无表情地悬在那里，他当然就笑场了。

990
00:43:27.060 --> 00:43:30.400
And then they figured out another way to bring me down, which was a leap down.
后来他们想出了另一种让我下来的方式，就是跳下来。

991
00:43:30.540 --> 00:43:38.100
But first, I would just – like one of the things we tried was just like being lowered down from the thing, which didn't make sense but was very funny.
但起初，我只是——我们尝试的方法之一就是被那样慢慢降下来，虽然不合逻辑，但非常搞笑。

992
00:43:38.100 --> 00:43:39.400
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

993
00:43:39.540 --> 00:43:40.220
I remember it.
我记得。

994
00:43:40.260 --> 00:43:40.820
I do, too.
我也记得。

995
00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:43.380
It was very weirdly Matrix-y.
那看起来有种诡异的《黑客帝国》感。

996
00:43:43.580 --> 00:43:44.140
It was.
确实。

997
00:43:44.220 --> 00:43:46.840
And Oscar was slowly coming.
而且奥斯卡是慢慢下来的。

998
00:43:47.260 --> 00:43:47.540
Like very slowly.
非常慢。

999
00:43:47.860 --> 00:43:51.480
What was that Tom Cruise movie where he slowly lowered himself down?
汤姆·克鲁斯那部他慢慢把自己降下来的电影叫什么来着？

1000
00:43:51.580 --> 00:43:52.360
Mission Impossible.
《碟中谍》。

1001
00:43:52.940 --> 00:43:53.720
It was like that.
当时就是那样。

1002
00:43:54.100 --> 00:43:56.800
Oscar was like slowly coming out of the ceiling.
奥斯卡就像是慢慢从天花板里钻出来一样。

1003
00:43:56.980 --> 00:43:58.460
It looked crazy.
看起来太疯狂了。

1004
00:43:58.800 --> 00:44:02.120
And Oscar, of course, did not break because he never broke.
当然，奥斯卡没有笑场，因为他从不笑场。

1005
00:44:02.320 --> 00:44:02.980
But we did.
但我们笑场了。

1006
00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:07.520
And all the rest of us were like, we can't possibly continue this if that's physically possible.
我们所有人都觉得，如果这种事在物理上是可能的，那我们根本没法继续拍下去。

1007
00:44:07.520 --> 00:44:10.300
And if Steve broke, you know it looked ridiculous.
而且如果史蒂夫笑场了，你知道那看起来有多荒谬。

1008
00:44:10.700 --> 00:44:14.480
Well, let me break it down for you for anyone who wants to follow along.
好吧，让我为想了解细节的人拆解一下。

1009
00:44:14.640 --> 00:44:20.880
At 2 minutes 38 seconds, the real Oscar is standing on his desk and he pushes up the ceiling tile.
在2分38秒时，真正的奥斯卡站在桌子上，推开了天花板的瓷砖。

1010
00:44:21.700 --> 00:44:29.860
At 2 minutes 43 seconds, for that beat of Oscar actually jumping up and pulling himself into the ceiling, that's his stunt double.
在2分43秒时，奥斯卡跳上去把自己拉进天花板的那一刻，那是他的替身演员。

1011
00:44:30.220 --> 00:44:30.860
You'll notice.
你会注意到的。

1012
00:44:31.040 --> 00:44:31.920
You don't see his face.
你看不到他的脸。

1013
00:44:32.220 --> 00:44:34.480
His double's name was Aladin Namu.
他的替身名字叫阿拉丁·纳穆。

1014
00:44:34.480 --> 00:44:41.300
And to pull this off, I guess Aladin had to wear a safety harness underneath his Oscar wardrobe.
为了完成这个动作，我猜阿拉丁必须在奥斯卡的戏服下穿上安全吊带。

1015
00:44:41.700 --> 00:44:49.640
And it had this cable that went up through his harness to a pulley that was manned by two guys in the ceiling.
吊带上连着一根缆绳，穿过滑轮，由天花板上的两个人操控。

1016
00:44:50.140 --> 00:44:54.440
And after he would jump, these guys would like hoist him up using this pulley.
他跳上去之后，这些人就会用滑轮把他拉上去。

1017
00:44:54.660 --> 00:44:56.940
You got to trust the guys in the ceiling, don't you?
你得信任天花板上的那些人，对吧？

1018
00:44:57.640 --> 00:45:01.940
Then at 2 minutes 48 seconds, we see the real Oscar again.
然后在2分48秒，我们又看到了真正的奥斯卡。

1019
00:45:02.140 --> 00:45:04.540
He's up there in the scaffold looking down.
他在上面的脚手架上往下看。

1020
00:45:04.780 --> 00:45:08.400
He was also secured by a harness and a cable, just to make sure.
为了保险起见，他也系着吊带和缆绳。

1021
00:45:09.400 --> 00:45:18.380
Finally, at 3 minutes 33 seconds, Oscar appears to break through another ceiling panel over by the kitchen near Creed's desk.
最后，在3分33秒，奥斯卡看起来撞破了厨房旁边克里德办公桌上方的另一块天花板。

1022
00:45:18.740 --> 00:45:20.840
That's his stunt double's legs kicking.
那是他替身演员踢腾的双腿。

1023
00:45:21.400 --> 00:45:24.920
Creed's reaction was so hilarious to me.
克里德的反应让我觉得太搞笑了。

1024
00:45:25.060 --> 00:45:25.740
Sorry, go on.
抱歉，你继续。

1025
00:45:25.740 --> 00:45:32.560
But at 4 minutes, 6 seconds, that is when the stunt team dropped real Oscar onto the floor.
但在4分06秒，那是特技团队把真正的奥斯卡扔到地板上的时候。

1026
00:45:32.840 --> 00:45:34.700
So many beats of the scene.
这一幕有太多节奏点了。

1027
00:45:34.840 --> 00:45:35.520
So many.
太多了。

1028
00:45:35.860 --> 00:45:39.480
We haven't even talked about Stanley's heart attack.
我们甚至还没聊到斯坦利的心脏病发作。

1029
00:45:39.680 --> 00:45:40.540
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1030
00:45:40.940 --> 00:45:43.340
At the end of all of this, he's on the ground.
这一切结束时，他躺在地上。

1031
00:45:44.540 --> 00:45:47.780
And Michael is like telling him he can't die.
迈克尔一直在告诉他不能死。

1032
00:45:47.900 --> 00:45:48.380
He can't die.
他不能死。

1033
00:45:48.380 --> 00:45:49.980
He's shoving a wallet in his mouth.
他往他嘴里塞了个钱包。

1034
00:45:50.100 --> 00:45:52.180
Yeah, Michael's yelling, Barack Obama's president.
没错，迈克尔大喊着，奥巴马是总统。

1035
00:45:52.180 --> 00:45:53.800
You can't die, Stanley.
你不能死，斯坦利。

1036
00:45:54.400 --> 00:45:56.660
We got a fan question from Megan G.
我们收到了一个来自梅根·G的粉丝提问。

1037
00:45:57.420 --> 00:46:04.560
Leslie David Baker spoke at my college and said that the scene where Michael puts the wallet in his mouth was improvised.
莱斯利·大卫·贝克在我的大学演讲时说，迈克尔往他嘴里塞钱包的那一幕是即兴发挥的。

1038
00:46:04.920 --> 00:46:06.120
Is this true?
这是真的吗？

1039
00:46:07.020 --> 00:46:09.080
Lady, I looked it up in the script.
女士，我查了剧本。

1040
00:46:09.260 --> 00:46:10.300
It is not there.
剧本里没有这一段。

1041
00:46:10.580 --> 00:46:14.480
It ended with him saying, you can't die, Barack Obama is president.
剧本结尾是他喊着，你不能死，奥巴马是总统。

1042
00:46:14.480 --> 00:46:17.460
That wallet bit was on the day.
塞钱包那段是拍摄当天加的。

1043
00:46:17.820 --> 00:46:18.940
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1044
00:46:19.260 --> 00:46:22.080
Well, I have a fan question that made me chuckle, Jenna.
好吧，我有一个让我忍俊不禁的粉丝提问，珍娜。

1045
00:46:22.780 --> 00:46:23.460
Emma N.
艾玛·N。

1046
00:46:23.720 --> 00:46:32.220
wrote in and said, Meredith has these kind of dirty, question mark, brown boots she's carrying at around 1 minute 49 seconds.
来信说，在1分49秒左右，梅瑞狄斯拿着一双看起来脏兮兮的棕色靴子。

1047
00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:37.700
And throughout some of the cold open, was there any deleted scene or explanation about this?
在整个开场戏中，有没有关于这个的删减片段或解释？

1048
00:46:37.700 --> 00:46:38.220
Oh.
哦。

1049
00:46:38.460 --> 00:46:39.980
Well, Emma, you got me curious.
好吧，艾玛，你勾起了我的好奇心。

1050
00:46:40.020 --> 00:46:41.760
I went to your time code.
我去看了一下你提到的时间点。

1051
00:46:41.940 --> 00:46:43.000
You are not wrong.
你说得没错。

1052
00:46:43.220 --> 00:46:44.040
I took a photo.
我拍了张照片。

1053
00:46:44.220 --> 00:46:45.580
Look, Jenna, I'll put it in stories.
你看，珍娜，我要把它发到快拍里。

1054
00:46:46.000 --> 00:46:46.820
What is it?
那是什么？

1055
00:46:50.660 --> 00:46:51.900
I recognize these boots.
我认得这双靴子。

1056
00:46:52.220 --> 00:46:59.840
I would bet money that those are Kate's Ugg boots that wardrobe gave us to keep under our desk when we were so cold.
我敢打赌，那是凯特穿的UGG雪地靴，当时我们太冷了，服装组让我们把它放在桌子底下。

1057
00:47:00.240 --> 00:47:02.080
They're not Meredith's boots.
那不是梅雷迪思的靴子。

1058
00:47:02.080 --> 00:47:03.780
So I texted Kate.
所以我给凯特发了条短信。

1059
00:47:04.740 --> 00:47:12.600
I said, Kate, in stress relief when Dwight almost burns down the building, did you grab your actual Ugg boots from under your desk?
我说，凯特，在《压力缓解》那一集里，德怀特差点把大楼烧了，你当时是不是从桌子底下拿走了你自己的UGG雪地靴？

1060
00:47:12.840 --> 00:47:13.940
Fans are asking.
粉丝们都在问呢。

1061
00:47:14.580 --> 00:47:18.540
And I sent her the picture and she wrote back, ha, ha, ha, I did.
我把照片发给她，她回我说，哈哈，是的。

1062
00:47:19.660 --> 00:47:23.760
So the direction we were given was clearly everyone's panicking and they're grabbing their things.
所以当时给我们的指示很明确，每个人都很恐慌，都在抓起自己的东西。

1063
00:47:23.760 --> 00:47:24.980
They want to get out of the building.
他们想逃出大楼。

1064
00:47:24.980 --> 00:47:27.320
And she said, I grabbed my Ugg boots.
她说，我抓起的是我的UGG雪地靴。

1065
00:47:27.460 --> 00:47:28.960
They are actually not dirty.
它们其实并不脏。

1066
00:47:29.080 --> 00:47:30.440
They're a dusty pink.
那是灰粉色的。

1067
00:47:30.780 --> 00:47:31.260
Oh.
噢。

1068
00:47:31.260 --> 00:47:32.600
So there you go, Emma.
所以就是这样，艾玛。

1069
00:47:32.800 --> 00:47:33.480
Nice catch.
观察得很仔细。

1070
00:47:34.060 --> 00:47:36.440
Lady, I think we should take a break.
女士，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

1071
00:47:36.680 --> 00:47:37.920
That's the cold open.
这只是开场戏。

1072
00:47:38.120 --> 00:47:39.460
That's just the cold open.
那仅仅是开场戏而已。

1073
00:47:39.580 --> 00:47:43.920
We still have this whole episode to break down and there is so much more to talk about.
我们还有整整一集要拆解，还有很多内容要聊。

1074
00:47:44.220 --> 00:47:44.760
All right.
好吧。

1075
00:47:44.860 --> 00:47:45.560
We'll be back.
我们马上回来。

1076
00:47:54.450 --> 00:47:55.530
We are back.
我们回来了。

1077
00:47:55.850 --> 00:48:03.190
Dwight and Michael are at a meeting in corporate because, um, hi, Dwight almost burned the building down and Stanley had a heart attack.
德怀特和迈克尔正在公司开会，因为，嗯，嗨，德怀特差点把大楼烧了，斯坦利还心脏病发作了。

1078
00:48:03.510 --> 00:48:08.150
So they're having to meet with David Wallace and Kendall from HR.
所以他们必须和大卫·华莱士以及人力资源部的肯德尔开会。

1079
00:48:08.150 --> 00:48:09.350
Yes, Kendall.
没错，是肯德尔。

1080
00:48:09.750 --> 00:48:10.730
Guest star alert.
客串明星预警。

1081
00:48:10.950 --> 00:48:12.750
Kendall was played by John Hartman.
肯德尔由约翰·哈特曼饰演。

1082
00:48:13.170 --> 00:48:14.610
Now we've heard of Kendall before.
我们之前听说过肯德尔。

1083
00:48:14.810 --> 00:48:19.950
He was mentioned in previous episodes and we heard his voice, remember, when he yelled at Holly.
他在之前的剧集里被提到过，我们也听过他的声音，记得吗，就是他冲霍莉大喊的时候。

1084
00:48:20.230 --> 00:48:21.010
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

1085
00:48:21.530 --> 00:48:23.370
So John Hartman did the voice.
所以约翰·哈特曼当时配了音。

1086
00:48:23.590 --> 00:48:24.810
And now here he is.
现在他本人也出场了。

1087
00:48:24.930 --> 00:48:25.870
He's at the table.
他坐在桌边。

1088
00:48:26.050 --> 00:48:27.050
He was so good.
他演得太好了。

1089
00:48:27.330 --> 00:48:31.510
You know that bit where they do the little runner where, like, take heed, heeded?
你知道他们那个小段子吗，就是关于“注意”和“注意到了”的那个梗？

1090
00:48:31.830 --> 00:48:33.830
Did you look it up to see if it was scripted?
你有查过那是剧本里写的吗？

1091
00:48:33.830 --> 00:48:36.990
I did because Sonia Y wanted to know.
我查了，因为索尼娅·Y想知道。

1092
00:48:37.510 --> 00:48:38.690
Sonia, so did I.
索尼娅，我也想知道。

1093
00:48:39.050 --> 00:48:40.390
It was scripted.
那是剧本写的。

1094
00:48:40.470 --> 00:48:45.630
It was scripted until the very last Michael heeded again.
直到最后迈克尔再次说出“注意到了”之前，都是剧本写的。

1095
00:48:46.270 --> 00:48:46.610
Yes.
是的。

1096
00:48:46.950 --> 00:48:48.370
They kind of added to the bit.
他们算是给那个段子加了点料。

1097
00:48:48.550 --> 00:48:52.490
Steve added to the bit at the very end, but everything else is scripted.
史蒂夫在最后给段子加了点东西，但其他部分都是剧本写的。

1098
